From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 09:36:59 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] netapi32: local accounts and local groups
 (NetUserAdd/Del/SetInfo, NetLocalGroup*, NetGroupAddUser)

Account changes go the way this system keeps accounts, for administrators only
(ERROR_ACCESS_DENIED otherwise):
- NetUserAdd / NetUserDel / NetUserSetInfo (password levels) are sg-admind
  requests (user-add, user-remove keep, user-password); a refusal is mapped to
  NERR_UserExists, NERR_PasswordTooShort, NERR_BadUsername, ERROR_LAST_ADMIN.
  Accounts are read from /etc/passwd and /etc/group (sgwine, sg-admins).
- Local group Administrators is the administrator accounts: adding or removing a
  local account is sg-admind user-type administrator|standard. Users is the
  standard accounts. Every other local group and every member that is not a
  local account is kept in the prefix registry (HKLM\Software\Wine\SG\LocalGroups)
  and changes no Unix group.
- NetLocalGroupAdd/Del/SetInfo/GetInfo/Enum/GetMembers (levels 0-3)/AddMember(s)/
  DelMember(s)/SetMembers with the documented errors (NERR_GroupNotFound,
  ERROR_ALIAS_EXISTS, ERROR_MEMBER_IN_ALIAS, ERROR_NO_SUCH_MEMBER,
  ERROR_MEMBER_NOT_IN_ALIAS, ERROR_SPECIAL_ACCOUNT for built-in groups); nothing
  changes when any member of a list is wrong.
- NetGroupAddUser: this computer is not a domain controller (NERR_NotPrimary).
Without sg-admind (a plain Wine) the old process-local user list stays.

Gate: test/fastnetacct-gate.sh with a stand-in sg-admind spool and /etc.
